1:1 COMMENT "# generator_listiter.z -- container iterator written as a generator."
1:69 EOL "\n"
2:1 COMMENT "#"
2:2 EOL "\n"
3:1 COMMENT "# Same shape as listiter.z's bag-with-iterator demo, but the"
3:61 EOL "\n"
4:1 COMMENT "# iteration is a generator instead of a hand-rolled BagIter class."
4:67 EOL "\n"
5:1 COMMENT "# Observable output matches listiter.z byte-for-byte."
5:54 EOL "\n"
6:1 COMMENT "#"
6:2 EOL "\n"
7:1 COMMENT "# Encapsulation: `public: unit { :count :iterate }` hides the"
7:62 EOL "\n"
8:1 COMMENT "# private fields a/b/c, and `BagWalk`'s field is"
8:49 EOL "\n"
9:1 COMMENT "# `Bag.private.borrow` so it can read them. `Bag.iterate` stays as"
9:67 EOL "\n"
10:1 COMMENT "# the public way in -- a thin factory declared `outx`, which is"
10:64 EOL "\n"
11:1 COMMENT "# what carries the pin from the generator's borrowed field out to"
11:66 EOL "\n"
12:1 COMMENT "# the caller's `b`."
12:20 EOL "\n"
13:1 COMMENT "#"
13:2 EOL "\n"
14:1 COMMENT "# A generator is a TYPE, so it is declared at unit level and named"
14:67 EOL "\n"
15:1 COMMENT "# in PascalCase like every other reftype. It cannot be nested inside"
15:69 EOL "\n"
16:1 COMMENT "# `Bag`'s `as` block: an inline type definition is refused there,"
16:66 EOL "\n"
17:1 COMMENT "# for a generator exactly as for a class."
17:42 EOL "\n"
18:1 EOL "\n"
